ta:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-18T13:17:23-08:00","id":1424810,"title":"","content":"Persuasion is, generally speaking the better Gift, but it depends a lot on the ST and how far they let its rather ill-defined increased effectiveness of social rolls go.<br /> <br /> Apecraft's Blessing can get you a better bonus, but it's for one roll per use, and lots of uses aren't going to need it. Other characters have traits to resist social rolls, fixing a tire isn't going to be difficult outside of high-stress situations. The car isn't rolling back at you after all.<br /> <br /> If Merits are in play, Ability Aptitude style Merits are easier on this concept since you can get a -2 to Crafts rolls in one go, leaving Persuasion to cover the many different social Abilities rather than trying to take a Merit for each (though there are some good social Merits too).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-18T15:36:16-08:00","id":1424822,"title":"","content":"What would a good craft ability be since cooking is a professional skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\"